# ====================================================================
# Azure Content Understanding - Experimental enableImage Flag Guide
# ====================================================================
#
# This guide demonstrates how to use the experimental enableImage flag
# to improve extraction accuracy for visually complex documents.
#
# PREREQUISITES:
# - Azure AI Content Understanding resource
# - GPT-4.1 model deployment (recommended for best results)
# - .env file with API_KEY and ENDPOINT_URL configured
#
# DOCUMENTATION:
# - Overview: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/content-understanding/overview
# - REST API: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/rest/api/contentunderstanding/operation-groups
#
# ====================================================================
#
# TABLE OF CONTENTS
# ====================================================================
# Use Ctrl+F (Windows) or Cmd+F (Mac) to jump to sections:
#
# SECTION 1: What is enableImage?
# SECTION 2: When to Use enableImage
# SECTION 3: Create Analyzer with enableImage
# SECTION 4: Analyze Documents
# SECTION 5: Comparing Results (With vs Without enableImage)
#
# ====================================================================

# Variables - Loaded from .env file in the same directory
@subscriptionKey = {{$dotenv API_KEY}}
@endpoint = {{$dotenv ENDPOINT_URL}}
@apiVersion = 2025-11-01

# ====================================================================
# SECTION 1: WHAT IS enableImage?
# ====================================================================
#
# The enableImage flag is a PRIVATE PREVIEW / EXPERIMENTAL feature that
# sends full-page rendered images to the GPT model IN ADDITION to the
# layout-based markdown extraction.
#
# How it works:
# 1. CU converts each PDF page to an image
# 2. Sends the image + layout markdown to GPT (e.g., GPT-4.1)
# 3. The model aggregates both channels for improved spatial understanding
#
# This combined input (OCR markdown + page images) improves extraction for:
# ✔ Two-column layouts (e.g., K-1 documents)
# ✔ Visually structured forms
# ✔ Documents where position, indentation, and grids matter
# ✔ Forms with checkbox layouts that depend on spatial context
#
# Internal testing showed improvements in specific fields (e.g., K-1 K3
# checkbox scenarios) with up to +8.7% accuracy improvement in some tests.
#
# ⚠️ IMPORTANT: This is an experimental feature. Results vary by document
# type and complexity. Always test with your specific documents.
#
# ====================================================================

# ====================================================================
# SECTION 2: WHEN TO USE enableImage
# ====================================================================
#
# ✔ RECOMMENDED FOR:
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# - Two-column layouts (e.g., K-1 tax documents)
# - Complex visual layouts where OCR text alone loses structure
# - Forms where field position determines meaning
# - Documents with boxed layouts, grids, or multi-column structures
# - Scenarios where VISUAL cues like labels, columns, or superscripts matter
#
# ✘ NOT RECOMMENDED WHEN:
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# - Latency is critical (extraction time may double, e.g., 55-60s → 119s)
# - You expect universal improvement (results are case-dependent)
# - Visual content is low-resolution
# - Simple single-column text documents (standard extraction works well)
#
# ====================================================================

# ====================================================================
# SECTION 3: CREATE ANALYZER WITH enableImage
# ====================================================================
#
# To use enableImage, create a custom analyzer with the _experimental
# configuration block. The flag must be set when creating the analyzer.
#
# 💡 TIP: Use GPT-4.1 for best results with image-based extraction.
#

### 3.1 Check current model deployments
# Ensure you have GPT-4.1 configured (recommended for enableImage)
GET {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/defaults?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

### 3.2 Create custom analyzer WITH enableImage enabled
# This analyzer is configured for visually complex documents like K-1 forms
# The _experimental.enableImage flag enables multimodal (image + markdown) processing
PUT {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_enableImage_analyzer1?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Custom analyzer with enableImage for two-column and visually complex documents",
  "baseAnalyzerId": "prebuilt-document",
  "models": {
    "completion": "gpt-4.1",
    "embedding": "text-embedding-ada-002"
  },
  "config": {
    "returnDetails": true,
    "enableOcr": true,
    "enableLayout": true,
    "enableFormula": true,
    "enableFigureDescription": true,
    "enableFigureAnalysis": true,
    "chartFormat": "chartjs",
    "disableContentFiltering": true,
    "tableFormat": "html",
    "estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence": true,
    "enableSegment": false,
    "omitContent": false,
    "segmentPerPage": false,
    "enableAnnotations": true,
    "annotationFormat": "markdown",
    "_experimental": {
      "enableImage": "true"
    }
  },
  "fieldSchema": {
    "fields": {
      "documentType": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "classify",
        "enum": ["K-1 Form", "Tax Form", "Financial Statement", "Other"],
        "description": "Classify this document as one of the following types based on its content, form number, and structure."
      },
      "taxYear": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The tax year shown on the document. Look for a four-digit year near labels like 'Tax Year', 'For calendar year', or in the form header. Format: YYYY (e.g., '2024')."
      },
      "partnerName": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The name of the partner or recipient. VISUAL: Look for the name field in the left column, typically near 'Part II - Information About the Partner' or labels like 'Partner's name'. Extract the full legal name."
      },
      "partnerSSN": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The partner's Social Security Number (SSN) or Tax Identification Number (TIN). VISUAL: Located near the partner name in the identification section, often labeled 'Partner's SSN or TIN' or 'Identifying number'."
      },
      "partnershipName": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The name of the partnership or entity issuing this K-1. VISUAL: Look in the header area or 'Part I - Information About the Partnership' section. Usually the first prominent name on the form."
      },
      "checkboxValues": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Checkbox status fields from the form. VISUAL: Carefully examine checkbox positions. Check marks may appear as X, ✓, filled boxes, or handwritten marks.",
        "properties": {
          "isFinalReturn": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "method": "extract",
            "description": "VISUAL: Check if the 'Final K-1' or 'Final return' checkbox is marked. Look for checkboxes near the top of the form or in Part I. Return true if marked, false if empty."
          },
          "isAmended": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "method": "extract",
            "description": "VISUAL: Check if the 'Amended K-1' checkbox is marked. Usually appears near 'Final K-1' checkbox. Return true if marked, false if empty."
          }
        }
      },
      "summary": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "generate",
        "description": "Generate a 2-3 sentence summary of the key financial information from this K-1 document, including the partnership name, partner name, tax year, and any notable distributions or allocations."
      }
    }
  }
}

### 3.3 Verify analyzer was created with enableImage
# Check that the _experimental.enableImage flag is present in the config
GET {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_enableImage_analyzer1?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

### 3.4 Create a COMPARISON analyzer WITHOUT enableImage
# Use this to compare results between image-enabled and standard extraction
PUT {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_noImage_analyzer?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Custom analyzer WITHOUT enableImage for comparison testing",
  "baseAnalyzerId": "prebuilt-document",
  "models": {
    "completion": "gpt-4.1",
    "embedding": "text-embedding-ada-002"
  },
  "config": {
    "returnDetails": true,
    "enableOcr": true,
    "enableLayout": true,
    "enableFormula": true,
    "enableFigureDescription": true,
    "enableFigureAnalysis": true,
    "chartFormat": "chartjs",
    "tableFormat": "html",
    "estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence": true,
    "enableAnnotations": true,
    "annotationFormat": "markdown"
  },
  "fieldSchema": {
    "fields": {
      "documentType": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "classify",
        "enum": ["K-1 Form", "Tax Form", "Financial Statement", "Other"],
        "description": "Classify this document as one of the following types based on its content, form number, and structure."
      },
      "taxYear": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The tax year shown on the document. Look for a four-digit year near labels like 'Tax Year', 'For calendar year', or in the form header. Format: YYYY (e.g., '2024')."
      },
      "partnerName": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The name of the partner or recipient. Look for labels like 'Partner's name' or 'Name' in the partner information section."
      },
      "partnerSSN": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The partner's Social Security Number (SSN) or Tax Identification Number (TIN). Located near the partner name, often labeled 'Partner's SSN or TIN' or 'Identifying number'."
      },
      "partnershipName": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "extract",
        "description": "The name of the partnership or entity issuing this K-1. Look in the header area or 'Part I - Information About the Partnership' section."
      },
      "checkboxValues": {
        "type": "object",
        "description": "Checkbox status fields from the form.",
        "properties": {
          "isFinalReturn": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "method": "extract",
            "description": "Check if the 'Final K-1' or 'Final return' checkbox is marked. Look for checkboxes near the top of the form. Return true if marked, false if empty."
          },
          "isAmended": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "method": "extract",
            "description": "Check if the 'Amended K-1' checkbox is marked. Usually appears near 'Final K-1' checkbox. Return true if marked, false if empty."
          }
        }
      },
      "summary": {
        "type": "string",
        "method": "generate",
        "description": "Generate a 2-3 sentence summary of the key financial information from this K-1 document, including the partnership name, partner name, tax year, and any notable distributions or allocations."
      }
    }
  }
}

# ====================================================================
# SECTION 4: ANALYZE DOCUMENTS
# ====================================================================
#
# ⏱️ LATENCY NOTE: enableImage processing takes longer than standard extraction.
# Expect approximately 2x processing time (e.g., 55-60s → 100-120s).
#
# 📋 TWO-STEP PROCESS (Long-running async operation):
# STEP 1: POST request initiates analysis (returns operation ID)
# STEP 2: GET request retrieves results using the operation ID
#

### 4.1 Analyze document WITH enableImage
# Replace the URL below with your document (K-1, multi-column form, etc.)
# @name enableImageAnalysis
POST {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_enableImage_analyzer1:analyze?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

{
  "inputs": [
    {
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure-Samples/azure-search-sample-data/refs/heads/main/sustainable-ai-pdf/Accelerating-Sustainability-with-AI-2025.pdf",
      "range": "1-3"
    }]
}

### 4.2 Get enableImage analysis results
# ⏱️ NOTE: May take 1-2 minutes for complex documents
# Poll this endpoint until status is "Succeeded"
GET {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzerResults/{{enableImageAnalysis.response.body.id}}?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

### 4.3 Analyze SAME document WITHOUT enableImage (for comparison)
# @name noImageAnalysis
POST {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_noImage_analyzer:analyze?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Content-Type: application/json
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

{
  "inputs": [
    {
      "url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Azure-Samples/azure-search-sample-data/refs/heads/main/sustainable-ai-pdf/Accelerating-Sustainability-with-AI-2025.pdf",
      "range": "1-3"
    }]
}

### 4.4 Get non-enableImage analysis results
GET {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzerResults/{{noImageAnalysis.response.body.id}}?api-version={{apiVersion}}
Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

# ====================================================================
# SECTION 5: COMPARING RESULTS & BEST PRACTICES
# ====================================================================
#
# After running both analyzers on the same document, compare:
# 1. Field accuracy - Are checkbox values correct?
# 2. Spatial fields - Are two-column fields properly separated?
# 3. Confidence scores - Check estimateFieldSourceAndConfidence values
# 4. Processing time - Note the latency difference
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BEST PRACTICES FOR SCHEMA DESIGN WITH enableImage
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Use VISUAL prefixes in field descriptions:
#    "VISUAL: Look for the checkbox in the upper-right corner"
#    "VISUAL: Refer to the image content for column positions"
#
# 2. For checkbox fields, describe the visual appearance:
#    "Check marks may appear as X, ✓, or filled boxes"
#
# 3. Reference spatial locations explicitly:
#    "Located in the left column, below the header"
#    "Found in Box 1 of Part III"
#
# 4. Test iteratively - change one variable at a time:
#    - First, test with enableImage OFF
#    - Then, test with enableImage ON
#    - Compare accuracy metrics between runs
#
# 5. Gather representative samples (3-5 minimum) and build ground truth
#    to objectively measure improvements
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Q: How do I confirm enableImage was applied?
# A: GET your analyzer definition (Section 3.3) and verify
#    _experimental.enableImage is present in the config
#
# Q: Results aren't improving with enableImage?
# A: Try adding VISUAL: prefixes to field descriptions to guide
#    the model to use image content. Some documents may not benefit.
#
# Q: Extraction is too slow?
# A: enableImage doubles processing time. Consider whether the
#    accuracy improvement justifies the latency for your use case.
#
# ====================================================================

### 5.1 Delete test analyzers (cleanup)
# Uncomment and run these when done testing

# DELETE {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_enableImage_analyzer1?api-version={{apiVersion}}
# Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

# DELETE {{endpoint}}/contentunderstanding/analyzers/custom_noImage_analyzer?api-version={{apiVersion}}
# Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key: {{subscriptionKey}}

# ====================================================================
